    "28": {
      "date": "2026-11-22",
      "edition": "Sunday 22 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Discipline meltdown",
          "heading": "Fiji Latui reduced to 12 men in nine-try rout by Ireland XV",
          "body": "Fiji's second-string Latui side conceded nine tries to an Ireland XV at Virgin Media Park on Friday, collecting four first-half yellow cards and, at one stage, playing with 12 men. Tighthead Mesake Doge was binned for a high tackle, then shown a second yellow — a 20-minute red card — 30 seconds after returning, for collapsing a scrum. Isaia Lotawa's no-arms tackle conceded a penalty try, and Apisalome Kuruisaqila was carded for a deliberate knock-on. Pita Lesivoukionoilau's intercept try, converted by Joeli Baleilevuka, gave the Latui their only lead."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Ireland beat Springboks 20-17 as Baloucoune scores twice",
          "body": "New Zealand: Beauden Barrett reaches 150 Tests as fourth man to do so. Erasmus faces possible ban breach after streaming Springboks loss."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "RTÉ Sport Rugby"
      }
    },
    "386": {
      "date": "2026-11-22",
      "edition": "Sunday 22 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Moody tribute",
          "heading": "Former captain Lewis Moody joins England to face the All Blacks' haka",
          "body": "Moody, diagnosed with motor neurone disease last year, stood between captain Maro Itoje and vice-captain Ellis Genge before Saturday's 37-12 win at Allianz Stadium, then delivered the match ball. Fellow vice-captains Ollie Chessum and Jamie George led the side forward into a V, and every England player wore boots bearing the logo of Moody's Front Up to MND campaign. Head coach Steve Borthwick said Moody had handed out the shirts the night before, telling BBC Radio 5 Live: \"It was some way to start a big game of rugby.\""
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Ireland beat Springboks 20-17 as Baloucoune scores twice",
          "body": "New Zealand: Beauden Barrett reaches 150 Tests as fourth man to do so. Fiji Latui reduced to 12 men in heavy loss to Ireland XV. Erasmus faces possible ban breach after streaming Springboks loss."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "BBC Rugby Union"
      }
    },
    "387": {
      "date": "2026-11-22",
      "edition": "Sunday 22 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Late change",
          "heading": "Jean-Baptiste Gros ruled out of Argentina test, Rodrigue Neti promoted to start",
          "body": "France loosehead Jean-Baptiste Gros was ruled out on Saturday of the Nations Championship meeting with Argentina after being judged too short of fitness. The Toulon forward had been excused training at Marcoussis on Wednesday, yet head coach Fabien Galthié still named him in the starting XV on Thursday. Toulouse's Rodrigue Neti, a replacement against South Africa, was named to start instead. Jefferson Poirot, who missed that Springbok win with concussion, stayed on the bench. Rugbyrama reported that Gros could miss the rest of the competition."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Ireland beat Springboks 20-17 as Baloucoune scores twice",
          "body": "New Zealand: Beauden Barrett reaches 150 Tests as fourth man to do so. Fiji Latui reduced to 12 men in heavy loss to Ireland XV. Erasmus faces possible ban breach after streaming Springboks loss."
