    "388": {
      "date": "2026-11-22",
      "edition": "Sunday 22 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Springboks beaten",
          "heading": "Robert Baloucoune scores twice as Ireland edge Springboks 20-17 in Dublin",
          "body": "Ulster wing Robert Baloucoune had Ireland ahead inside eight minutes of Saturday's Nations Championship test at the Aviva Stadium, then crossed again before the break. Two missed Sam Prendergast conversions let South Africa draw level, but Rónan Kelleher's try in the corner made it 17-10 at half-time. A Prendergast penalty stretched the lead before Malcolm Marx's Springbok try, with just over 20 minutes left, set up a nervy finish. Balls.ie notes it is Ireland's first win over South Africa, France or New Zealand since July 2024."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "New Zealand: Beauden Barrett reaches 150 Tests as fourth man to do so",
          "body": "Fiji Latui reduced to 12 men in heavy loss to Ireland XV. Erasmus faces possible ban breach after streaming Springboks loss."
        }
      ]
    },
    "389": {
      "date": "2026-11-22",
      "edition": "Sunday 22 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Injury blow",
          "heading": "Prop Simone Ferrari ruled out of Fiji defeat an hour before kick-off",
          "body": "OnRugby reports that tighthead Simone Ferrari injured his left arm during the build-up in Udine, and his recovery time will be assessed in the coming days. Marco Riccioni, originally named on the bench, was promoted to the No. 3 shirt, and fellow tighthead Ion Neculai came into the 23 at 18. The reshuffled side, captained by hooker Giacomo Nicotera, went down 16-21 to Fiji. It was a sixth loss in six, and it leaves Italy 12th of 12 on the log."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
