          "kicker": "Roll of honour",
          "heading": "WRU counts 68 Wales players to beat All Blacks after Cardiff win",
          "body": "The 23 men who beat New Zealand 35-28 at Principality Stadium on 14 November have taken the roll of Wales players to have beaten the All Blacks from 45 to 68, the Welsh Rugby Union has noted. They join the sides of 1905, 1935 and 1953. The WRU also points out that fans celebrated in the same Cardiff pubs as after those earlier wins, the City Arms, the Angel Hotel and Queen's Vaults among them. A celebratory pint, it adds, has risen from 1½p in 1905 to around £5.25."
        },
